Chromium 157.0.8103.30 -> 157.0.8103.32, for the 157.0.8103.30 tarball.

157.0.8103.32 is a tag on the 157 branch (refs/branch-heads/8103) that has
no source tarball (as of 2026-10-29). It has fixes made after
157.0.8103.30: use-after-frees in the bookmarks side panel and MojoCdm;
HttpCache rejecting overlong range responses; File System Access's
blocklist of sensitive paths; re-entry when draining error events; layer
changes during a commit; nested printing; menu items deleted while being
inserted; relatedTarget's cross-origin check; V8's code generator and
deoptimization data; Skia's SkSL parser and GL BGRA formats. Some are
likely security fixes that later release notes will credit.

Generated from the upstream diffs between the tags (chromium/src
refs/tags/157.0.8103.30..157.0.8103.32, 23 commits), Skia and V8 (the only
dependencies whose DEPS revisions changed; no CIPD/GCS package or gclient
gn arg changed), from blobless git fetches, with
scripts/chromium-delta/filter.py.

Left out, as they cannot affect a Linux build: files not in the release
tarball, iOS/Android/ChromeOS/Mac/Windows-only files, tests and docs,
PGO pointers, submodule pointer updates, DEPS.

Added: the tarball's stamp files for the new commit (stamps.py:
build/util/LASTCHANGE{,.committime}, gpu/config/gpu_lists_version.h and
skia/ext/skia_commit_hash.h; commit
19debac871c8f51d98fce4c22bd211d2e1718498, refs/branch-heads/8103@{#966}).
Dawn's stamps and build/util/MINIBRANCH don't change.

Checked: applies to the 157.0.8103.30 tarball; chrome/VERSION becomes
157.0.8103.32; every patched source file is byte-identical to its version
at the tag; the 157.0.8103.30 tarball's non-git files are all classified
(tarball-generated.py with generated.conf).

Apply with git apply.

